Recall handler deadline + bounded worker drain, for the Hindsight HA add-on.

Applied in the Dockerfile with `patch -p1 -d /app/api` against the API package
COPY-ed from the digest-pinned upstream image (v0.7.1 / 779e3140; the package
is an editable install, so the source lives at /app/api/hindsight_api). When
bumping HINDSIGHT_IMAGE, regenerate this patch against the new source — the
build fails loudly here if the context drifts.

Two changes, both no-ops unless their env var is set:

1. api/http.py api_recall: wrap recall_async in asyncio.wait_for when
   HINDSIGHT_API_RECALL_HANDLER_TIMEOUT (seconds) > 0. On expiry the recall
   task is cancelled and the pre-existing `except (asyncio.TimeoutError,
   TimeoutError)` branch returns 504, so callers fail fast instead of the
   server silently working past the caller's own timeout (observed on the
   N150: aborted clients leave doomed work running to completion, so queues
   grow without bound during busy evenings).

2. api/http.py lifespan: make the worker poller drain timeout configurable
   via HINDSIGHT_API_WORKER_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT (was hardcoded 30.0s). With the
   HA Supervisor's default 10s docker-stop grace (config.yaml `timeout`), a
   30s drain guaranteed SIGKILL (exit 137) whenever consolidation/retain was
   in flight at stop time — e.g. every nightly cold backup. In-flight worker
   tasks are re-queued/retried after restart, so a short drain is safe.

--- a/hindsight_api/api/http.py	2026-07-12 08:18:32.288595189 +0200
+++ b/hindsight_api/api/http.py	2026-07-12 08:19:24.277470245 +0200
